<title>UK: BOE gives UK money market 205 mln stg late help.</title>
<headline>BOE gives UK money market 205 mln stg late help.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-02-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bank of England said it provided the UK money market with around 205 million stg of unspecified late assistance.  </p>
<p>			    EARLY	1200 GMT   1400 GMT   LATE</p>
<p> FORECAST SHORTAGE    1.05 BLN   1.05 BLN   1.0 BLN    1.0 BLN</p>
<p> CUMULATIVE SUPPLY    25 MLN     189 MLN    630 MLN    835 MLN</p>
<p> DETAILS</p>
<p> BAND 1  BANK BILLS   =	    =	    187 MLN*   =</p>
<p> BAND 2  BANK BILLS   =	    =	    254 MLN*   =</p>
<p> BILLS TO MARCH 3     25 MLN#    164 MLN#    =	   =</p>
<p> UNSPECIFIED ASSISTANCE					  205 MLN</p>
<p> * INTEREST RATE - 5-15/16 PCT (INDICATES UNCHANGED BASE RATES)</p>
<p> ! INTEREST RATE - 5-31/32 PCT (INDICATES UNCHANGED BASE RATES)</p>
</text>
